hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2385","Sayyiduna Shareed (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked that my mother (Sahiba) owes the expiation of freeing a neck and I have a black Abyssinian slave girl, will she be enough? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Call her and bring her.\" When she came, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \"Do you testify that there is no god but Allah?\" He said: Yes, he said: \"Go and set her free. She is a believer.\""
"2386","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"Your oath will be based on what your Sahib (companion) considers you to be truthful.\""
"2387","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The oath of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, was like this: \"Laa wa muqalib al-qulubbi\", not the oath of the one who turns hearts, \"And Allah knows best.\""
"2388","Sayyiduna Abu Sharh al-Khuza'i (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \"Whoever is bled or injured, he (or his heir) has the right to accept one of three things. If he wants to do the fourth thing, stop him. These are the three things: either he asks for retribution (killing for murder), or he forgives, or he takes death, then he chooses one of these three things. Fourthly, if he does more than that, then for him (the heir) is the fire of hell where he will remain forever."
"2389","It was narrated from Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm on the authority of Abia on the authority of Jeddah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, wrote a decree for the people of Yemen, and in this letter it was: \"Whoever kills a Muslim without reason and the witnesses prove that blood is on him, qisas is obligatory on him (i.e. he will be avenged) unless the heirs of the deceased agree.\" (i.e. forgive). \n Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: \"Atbat\" means to kill for some excuse."
"2390","Sahl bin Abi Hatmah said: Abdullah bin Sahl bin Abi Hatmah, a member of Banu Haritha, went to Khyber with some people of his people in search of livelihood, Abdullah was raped, he was killed, his neck was twisted and the seals (beads) were broken (i.e. his neck was badly crushed) and his body was thrown into one of the springs of Khyber, his companions shouted and took out his body. Then those people came to Madinah Tayyaba to serve the Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Sahl, may God bless him and grant him peace, the brother of the deceased, who was an old companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his cousins, Hawaisah and Muhaisa Ibna Masud, were with him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: \"Let the elders speak\", so they withdrew and Hawaisah and Muhaisa spoke again, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: \"Tell the name of the murderer, then swear fifty times (that he is the murderer) and we will hand over this murderer to you.\" He said: O Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him! How can we swear on what we do not know? We don't know who killed them. Yes, it is certain that the Jews are our enemies and they have been killed among them. He said: \"Then they (Jews) will have to swear that they are innocent of the murder of your victim (i.e. they did not kill) then they will be acquitted.\" He said: We will not believe the oaths of the Jews because they often swear falsely. Pay it."
"2391","It was narrated from Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm on the authority of Abiyyah on the authority of Jeddah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a letter to the people of Yemen that said: \"A man should be killed in exchange for a woman.\""
"2392","It was narrated on the authority of Anas that a girl's head was crushed between two stones. Even when the Jew's name was mentioned, he nodded his head in support, so he was called and he confessed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered and his head was also crushed between two stones."
"2393","Abu Juhaifa said: I asked Sayyiduna Ali (RA): O Commander of the Faithful! Do you have anything other than the Book of Allah as a revelation? (i.e. that which is not in the Holy Qur'an), he said: No, by the One who split the grain and created the soul, I do not know anything except the Qur'an except the understanding (and insight) which Allah bestows upon whom He wills of His Book, and which is written in the leaf. I said: What is written in this leaf? He said: The commandments of the day and the release of prisoners and the issue that a Muslim should not be killed in exchange for an infidel."
"2394","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Do not set limits (punishments) inside the mosque, nor should a father be killed in exchange for his son.\""
"2395","On the authority of Sayyidna Samura bin Jundab, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever kills his slave, We will kill him as revenge, and whoever cuts off his nose, We will cut off his nose.\" The narrator said: Then Hasan, may God have mercy on him, forgot this hadith and used to say: A free man will not be killed in exchange for a slave."
"2396","Sayyiduna Wail bin Hajar (RA) said: I was in the service of the Prophet (PBUH) at that time. A murderer was brought to him tied with a belt. The Prophet (PBUH) said to the guardian of the deceased: \"Will you forgive this murderer?\" He said: No, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Then people?\" He said: \"Then you will kill him?\" He said: Yes, I will kill. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"If you forgive this murderer, it will take away your sin and that of your murdered (brother)\"."
"2397","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The major sins are: associating partners with Allah, disobeying parents, taking someone's life unjustly\" - Shu'ba doubted - or \"swearing falsely.\""
"2398","On the authority of Sayyidna Thabit bin Dahhak, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Cursing a believer is equivalent to murder, and the person who commits suicide with something in this world will be punished with that thing on the Day of Resurrection.\""
"2399","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “He who commits suicide with an iron will have that weapon in his hand which he will keep barking in his stomach, and will remain forever in the Hellfire, and whoever commits suicide by eating poison, his poison will be in his hand which he will always drink in the Hellfire, and whoever kills himself by falling from a mountain will always fall into the Hellfire. Will do."
"2400","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: A man killed a man during the time of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, set his death penalty at 12,000 dirhams. They could not do it, and those disbelievers were not angry except because Allah and the Messenger made them rich out of His bounty (At-Tawbah: 74/9) i.e. by taking money."
"2401","On the authority of Sayyidna Amr bin Hazm, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to the people of Yemen: \"The duet on those who sleep is one thousand dinars.\" (i.e. those who have gold)"
"2402","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Amr bin Hazm that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote in the letter that he sent to the people of Yemen: \"In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, this is a letter from the Prophet of Muhammad, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, to Sharahbeel bin Abdulkalal, Harith bin Abdulkalal, Na'eem bin Abdulkalal, Qayl Dhi Ra'in, Maafar, and Hamdan, that the death penalty for killing one soul is a hundred camels.\""
"2403","Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm narrated on the authority of his father from his grandfather (Sayyidna Amr bin Hazm, may God be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to the people of Yemen, in which it was written: \"And there is a full amount of money in the nose when you cut it from the root, and a full money in the tongue, lips, testicles, zikr (special organ) and the back, in both eyes there is a full money, half of a toe, in a wound of the brain and one in the stomach.\" A third is worth, and a wound that breaks a bone is worth fifteen camels."
"2404","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, defined the crime of murder as five types."
"2405","It was narrated from Imran bin Hussain (RA) that the slave of the poor cut off the hand of the slave of the rich. His owner came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH). The people said: O Messenger of Allah (PBUH)! This slave belongs to the faqirs (i.e. those who cannot pay dowry), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not impose anything (duet) on them."
"2406","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Musa Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The fingers are all equal.\" Sayyidina Abu Musa said: There are ten (on each finger). He said: \"Yes.\""
"2407","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"This and these (all) are equal\" and pointed to the finger and thumb."
"2408","Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm narrated from his grandfather on the authority of his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to the people of Yemen that: \"For every finger and toe there are ten camels (dayat).\""
"2409","Amr ibn Shuaib narrated from his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, prescribed a diet of five camels for wounds that reach the bone."
"2410","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm narrated from his grandfather on the authority of his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to the people of Yemen: \"And there are ten camels in each finger and toe, and there are five camels in each finger and toe.\""
"2411","Amr ibn Shuaib narrated from his father and then from his grandfather: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided on the diet of five camels in their teeth."
"2412","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad Amr bin Hazm narrated from his grandfather on the authority of his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote for the people of Yemen: \"And there are five camels in the tooth.\""
"2413","It was narrated from Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) that a man bit a man's hand with a tooth, so he pulled his hand from the biter's mouth, which broke two of his front teeth. Then he brought his dispute to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), and the Prophet (PBUH) said: \"You bite your own brother with the tooth like a camel bites, go, you will not get any money.\""
"2414","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"If a chopper injures someone, his blood will not be shed, no blood will be shed for falling into a well, no blood will be shed for being buried in an ear, and there is a fifth part in burial.\""
"2415","It has been narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) in this chain of transmission as mentioned above."
"2416","It has been narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) in this chain of transmission as mentioned above."
"2417","On the authority of Sayyidna Mugheera bin Shuba, may Allah be pleased with him, he narrates from the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that two women were married to the same man, one of them had a disagreement due to the other's honor, so one of them struck the other with an iron rod, as a result of which the other woman died and her unborn child also died. He put this woman's money on the woman's aqeela."
"2418","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrated that Sayyidna Umar ibn al-Khattab (may God be pleased with him) sought the decision of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the fetus, and Hamal ibn Malik ibn Nabagha stood up and said: I was in the middle of two women. He ordered the killing of the woman who had beaten her, that is, by declaring it a premeditated murder, he decided to kill the woman in revenge."
"2419","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira that two women of Hazail tribe fought and one hit the other with a stone, which killed her and what was in her stomach also perished. The heirs of the murdered woman brought this dispute to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of God be upon him, so he decided on a slave or a concubine instead of the fetus (abdomen) and placed the dowry of the murdered woman on the relatives of the murdered woman, and declared the heirs of this dowry to the children and husband of the murdered woman, etc. At that time, Hamal bin Nabagha Hazli said: O Messenger of God! How should we reward a child who neither drank, nor ate, nor spoke, nor shouted, such an order is not reliable. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"This is evident from the brothers of the priests, because he rhymed like the priests.\""
"2420","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The body of a person killed by a crime or suspect, which is (killed) with a whip and a stick (one hundred camels), including forty camels with babies in their bellies.\" (i.e. pregnant)."
"2421","Sayyidna Sahl bin Saad al-Saadi, may God be pleased with him, reported that a man began to look in through a hole in the door of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had an iron comb in his hand at that time, with which he, may God bless him and grant him peace, was combing his head. He said: \"The order to take permission has been given so as not to be seen.\""
"2422","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Saad (RA) said: When the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was combing his hair with an iron comb in the room, one of the Companions started peeking in. The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"If I had known that you were peeking, I would have stood up and poked the comb in your eye. Permission has been ordered for the sake of sight.\""
"2423","Sayyiduna Muti' (may Allah be pleased with him) said: On the day of the conquest of Makkah, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: \"After today, no Quraysh will be tied and killed until the Day of Resurrection.\""
"2424","It has been narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Muti, may Allah be pleased with him, and the translation is the same as mentioned above. \n Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: In the commentary of the above mentioned hadith, the scholars have said that it means that all Qureshi will become Muslims and no one will die in disbelief, that is, from now on, no Qureshi will remain a disbeliever and if he commits a crime, he will be killed."
"2425","Sayyiduna Abu Musa said: I came to Madinah with my son. We did not see the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him. I went to him, he came out wearing double clothes. I said: By the Lord of the Kaaba, this is my boy. He said: \"Is this your son?\" He said: Yes, I give his testimony (or you be a witness, this is my son). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Surely your son will not be responsible for your sins and crimes, and neither will you be responsible for his sins and crimes.\""
"2426","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (RA) said: I attended the service of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) with my father, and he (PBUH) said to my father: \"Is this your son?\" He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba, he said: \"Are you telling the truth?\" He said: Yes, in truth, I give his testimony (that this is my son). Abu Musa said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, smiled and laughed at my father's resemblance to him and my father's oath and said: \"Surely, this son of yours will not be responsible for your crime, nor will you be responsible for his crime.\" 164/6 and Israa: 15/17)."
"2427",""
"2428","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"Whoever knowing the truth of Allah's word and going out for Jihad in the way of Allah only with the intention of Jihad, Allah is his guarantor. Either Allah will make him a martyr and enter Paradise, or else He will bring this mujahid back to his home with reward and booty.\""
"2429","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah (PBUH)! Which is the best Jihad? He said: \"That Jihad is the best in which the mujahid's horse is killed and its blood is shed\", (i.e. in which the mujahid sacrifices his life and wealth in the way of Allah and becomes a martyr)."
"2430","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was asked: Which is the best deed? He said: \"Believing in Allah and His Messenger.\" It was asked: Which action is better after that? He said: \"Doing Jihad in the way of Allah.\" It was asked: Then which action is better? He said: \"Hajj Mabarur.\""
"2431","Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"He who fights in the way of Allah until a camel milks twice, Jannah has become obligatory for him. And this is such a period that the milker milks the milk and the camel gives up its milk.\""
"2432","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) passed by those who were sitting. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Shall I not tell you the person who is the best in the sight of Allah?\" He said: Surely, he said: \"The person who takes his horse and goes out in the way of Allah (i.e. does jihad) until he dies or is martyred.\" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"After that, the person who is close to him in action, shall I tell you?\" He said: O Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace! He said: \"Then there is a person who separates from people and prays in a valley, gives zakat and stays away from people's wickedness and evils, and shall I not tell you who is the worst?\" We said: Tell me. He said: \"A person who is asked in the name of Allah and does not give anything (this is the worst person).\" It is in some hadiths that a person who asks in the name of Allah and is not given anything)."
"2433","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever stands in a row in the way of Allah, his rank and position and his standing are better than a person's worship for sixty years.\""
"2434","It was narrated from Abdullah bin Sulaiman that Malik bin Abdullah passed by Habib bin Muslimah or Habib passed by Malik who was walking on foot holding his horse. He said: Why don't you get on board? May Allah guide you, said: Verily the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever has both his feet dusted in the way of Allah, Allah has forbidden the Hellfire for him.\""
"2435","On the authority of Sayyiduna Sahl bin Saad, may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"A morning spent in the way of Allah or an evening spent in the way of Allah is better than anything in the world.\""
"2436","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever fasts one day in the way of Allah for the sake of Allah, Allah will remove him from Hellfire at a distance of seventy years.\""
"2437","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Rihanah that he was in a battle with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he heard him saying: \"Forbidden to Hell is the eye that wakes up in the way of Allah, and forbidden to Hell is that eye that becomes tearful (i.e. filled with tears) from the fear of Allah.\" I forgot it. Abu Shareeh said: I heard from the narrator who mentioned the third eye and that is: \"Allah has forbidden Hellfire for an eye that avoids the sight of Allah's mahram\" (i.e. does not see obscene things or such an eye that is torn (i.e. lost) in the way of Allah the Exalted)."
"2438","On the authority of Sayyidna Uqbah bin Amir Jahni (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \"May Allah have mercy on the guard of the army.\" \n Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: In the chain of this hadith, the meeting of Umar bin Abdul Aziz with Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (RA) is not proven."
"2439","Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A companion came with a camel with a mahar (nickel) and said that it is (a gift) in the way of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"On the Day of Resurrection, there will be seven hundred camels for you (instead of this one), all of which will be rich.\""
"2440","Sa'sa' bin Mu'awiya said: I met Sayyidna Abu Dharr who was carrying his camel and a musket was hanging around his neck. I said: O Abu Dharr! what is it what happened to you He said: This is my job. I then asked: What has happened to you? Then he replied: This is my job. I said: Narrate any such hadith that you have heard from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \"Whoever spends (gives) a couple of rupees in the way of Allah, the gatekeepers of Paradise will hasten to receive him.\" \n It is in the tradition of Nasa'i that \"the gatekeepers of Paradise will call him to them\" (to enter through their gate). Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: \"Couple\" means: two dirhams or two slaves, two slaves, or two horses."
"2441","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (may Allah be pleased with him) recited this noble verse (translation): \"Prepare for the disbelievers as much force as you can. Listen: Force means: shooting arrows.\""
"2442","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “Allah the Exalted will admit three men to Paradise because of one arrow, the one who made the arrow if he had a good intention in making it, the one who helped him and the one who wielded the arrow.” Then the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “Archery, ride, and to me archery is more beloved than riding.” To shoot, and to train a horse, and to play with one's wife, these three sports are right.\" And he said: \"Whoever abandons shooting after learning it has been ungrateful to the one who taught him.\""
"2443","Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"Whoever is injured in the way of Allah, the Exalted and Exalted, Allah will raise him up on the Day of Resurrection in such a way that blood will flow from his wound, the smell of which will be like musk, and the color will be exactly like blood.\""
"2444","Sahl bin Umama bin Sahl bin Hanif narrated a hadith from his grandfather through his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever asks for martyrdom with a sincere heart, Allah will raise him to the rank of martyrs, even if he dies in his bed.\""
"2445","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"A martyr suffers as much from being killed as one of you suffers from an ant bite.\""
"2446","Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"There is no soul who dies and enters Paradise, then wishes to return to you (to the world) except a martyr who wishes to be killed repeatedly for the reward of martyrdom.\""
"2447","Masrooq, may Allah have mercy on him, said that we asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, about the souls of the martyrs. And if it was not for Sayyiduna Abdullah (RA), he would not have told us any Hadith. He said: The souls of the martyrs will be in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection in the form of green birds, which will live in lanterns hanging from the Throne, and will move about wherever they want in Paradise, and then return to their lanterns. Their Lord (Lord of the Worlds) will look at them and ask: \"Do you need anything?\" Those spirits will say: We do not need anything else except to return to the world and then be killed again (i.e. martyred)."
"2448","Utbah bin Abdul Salmi said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"There are three types of those who are killed: (1) A believer who fought with his life and wealth in the way of Allah, and when he was surrounded by the enemy, he fought and was killed\". (2) \"The second is the believer whose good and bad deeds are mixed, he fought in the cause of Allah with his life and wealth, when he was crowded by the enemy, he fought until he was killed.\" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about such a deceased person: \"It is a sucking object that erases his sins and sins, because the sword is an eraser of sins, such a deceased person will be admitted through any gate of Paradise.\" (3) \"The third victim is the hypocrite who waged Jihad with his life and wealth. When he met the enemy, he fought a (good) battle and was killed, but he will go to hell and the sword will not be able to erase (the stain of) hypocrisy.\" \n Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: When the cloth is washed and thrown away, it is called Musus. Hence the meaning of masamsa: washed thing."
"2449","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and gave a sermon: Praise and worship of Allah, then he mentioned Jihad, and he did not leave anything that is better than Jihad (i.e. said Jihad to be the best) except duties. A Companion stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah! Tell me, if a person is killed in the way of Allah, will his mistakes be forgiven? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Yes, whoever is killed with patience with the intention of reward, if he is killed while advancing and not retreating (all his sins will be forgiven), except for the debt, he will be impeached even after he is martyred, as Gabriel (peace be upon him) has just told me.\""
"2450","It was narrated from Sayyidna Safwan bin Umayyah that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The plague (dying) is martyrdom, drowning (drowning) is also martyrdom, dying while fighting is martyrdom, abdominal pain (dying) is martyrdom, and the death of pregnant women is martyrdom.\""
"2451","Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"Fighting in the way of Allah is martyrdom, plague is martyrdom, stomach (stomach disease) is martyrdom, and if a pregnant woman dies because of the fetus, this is martyrdom.\""
"2452","Sayyidna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We used to participate in the Ghazwat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). At that time, we had nothing to eat except the leaves of the tree. We were treated like goats, that is, we were not mixed (treated like magnii). (Samar and Warak al-Hablah refer to the leaves of the tree)."
"2453","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Ubadah bin Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever does Jihad in the way of Allah and has no intention in his struggle but a rope, he will get the same thing.\""
"2454","Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"There are two kinds of Jihad, the one who fought for the sake of Allah, obeyed the Imam (i.e. his officer and chief) and spent what he liked, was gentle with his companion and refrained from temptation and mischief, then his sleeping will be a reward for everything, and the one who fights for the sake of boasting and boasting, disobeys the Amir, on earth.\" If he creates mischief, he will not return to the same level.\" (That is, there is neither reward nor punishment, so it is difficult for him to return, rather he will be caught in punishment.)"
"2455","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever does not fight jihad, does not provide goods for the mujahid, and does not follow the mujahid with trust and guard his family, Allah will afflict him with calamity and trouble before the Day of Judgment.\""
"2456","It was narrated from Sayyidna Zaid bin Khalid al-Jahni that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever gives equipment to a warrior in the way of Allah and guards the household of a Ghazi behind him in a benevolent way, Allah Almighty writes for him the reward of Mujahid and Ghazi, and nothing is diminished from the reward of the Ghazi.\""
"2457","Sayyidna Bara bin Azib (RA) says that when this noble verse: “(﴿La Yastwi al-Qa’idun ........... Alkh)” was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) called Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (RA) and he came with a broad shoulder bone and wrote down this verse. (Verse: Surah Nisa: 95/4)."
"2458","Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) said: (His aunt) Sayyida Umm Haram bint Malhan (RA) narrated to me a hadith that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) said Qilaula one day in her house, and when he woke up, he was laughing. What made you laugh? He said: \"I saw (in a dream) some people of my ummah riding on this sea (for Jihad) like kings riding on the throne.\" I said: Pray for me too, that Allah may make me one of them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"You will be one of them.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah! What are you laughing at? He said: \"I saw some people of my people who will ride on this sea like a king who ascends the throne.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah! Pray, may Allah make me one of them. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"You will be from the first group.\" \n The narrator said: She (Sayyida Umm Haram, may God be pleased with her) was married by Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit, may God be pleased with her, and he took her to join the sea fleet, and on the way back, a horse was brought near for her to ride on, but she fell and crushed her neck, and she died."
"2459","Sayyidah Umm Atiya (Nusiba bint Al-Harith) said: I participated in seven campaigns with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"2460","Sayyida Ayesha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out, he used to draw lots for the names of his wives."
"2461","Abu Salih, a freed slave of Sayyidna Uthman (RA) said: I heard Ameerul Momineen Sayyidna Uthman (RA) saying on the pulpit: I hid from you a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) so that you would not leave me. They were: \"To guard one day in the way of Allah is better than a thousand years and than to guard houses.\""
"2462","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \"The chain of deeds of every dead person ends except the one who guards the path of Allah, his chain of deeds continues until he is resurrected.\""
"2463","Sayyiduna Urwa al-Barqi, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Goodness and blessings will be tied to the foreheads of horses until the Day of Resurrection, meaning that they will be the cause of reward in the Hereafter and booty in this world.\""
"2464","The previous example is mentioned in this document as well. The translation of the tradition has been mentioned above."
"2465","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, a companion said: O Messenger of Allah! I want to buy a horse, so which horse should I buy? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \"Buy a black horse with white on the nose and upper lip, and white on the hands and feet, only the right hand is not white, or buy a black reddish horse with these marks, you will also get booty and (by God) you will be safe.\""
"2466","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to make dangerous horses race from Hafia to Sania, and he used to make harmless horses race from Sania to Masjid Bani Zariq. And Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) was also among those who participated in this horse race."
"2467","Abul Baid said: During the governorship of Hajjaj and Haqm bin Ayyub at Basra, there was a horse race. So we went to meet him, he was in his palace in Zawiya at that time, we asked him and said: O Abu Hamza! Did you people bet on horses during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? And he said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, also used to make bets. Sayyidina Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: Yes, by Allah, the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) placed a bet on his horse, which was called Sabha, and it won over everyone, and he (may God's prayers and peace be upon him) was very happy about it and he liked it very much. \n Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: \"Anhishah\" means \"amazing\"."
"2468","On the authority of Sayyidina Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Fight Jihad against the polytheists with your lives, wealth, and tongues.\""
"2469","Sayyiduna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"A group of my ummah will always prevail over the people until the command of Allah comes (i.e. death or resurrection) and even then they will prevail.\""
"2470","Ameerul Momineen Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \"Some people of my Ummah will always stick to the truth.\""
"2471","Sayyidna Abu Dharr Ghafari (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"After me there will be a nation in my ummah who will recite the Qur'an and will not descend from their circles (i.e. they will be inactive), they will depart from the religion like an arrow from the bow, and they will not return to the religion, they are the worst of all creation.\" \n Sulaiman said: Hameed said: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Samit (may God be pleased with him) said: Then I met Sayyidna Rafi’ bin Amr al-Ghafari, the brother of Haqm bin Amr al-Ghafari, and narrated this hadith."
"2472","On the authority of Sayyiduna Sakhar al-Ghamdi, may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \"O Allah, bless my Ummah in the early hours of the morning\", and when the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, would send out an army, he would send them out only in the morning. \n The narrator said: And this person (narrator of Hadith Sayyiduna Sakhr) was a merchant and used to send his servants (for trading) in the morning, which greatly blessed his property and increased his wealth."
"2473","Sayyidna Ka'b bin Malik (RA) said: It would have been rare that when the Messenger of Allah (SAW) intended to travel, he would have left on a day other than Thursday."
"2474","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The best companions (travelling companions) in the sight of Allah are those who are good to their companions, and the best neighbor in the sight of Allah is the one who is good to his neighbor.\""
"2475","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The best companions are four, and the best army is the one with four thousand men, and the best army is the one with four hundred men, and if the number becomes twelve thousand and they act patiently and truthfully, they will not be defeated because of scarcity.\""
"2476","Salman bin Buraidah narrated from his father, Sayyiduna Buraidah, may Allah be pleased with him: He said: When the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed a commander of a platoon, he used to command him that he himself should fear Allah and treat the Muslims who are with him with fear of Allah. Do not betray, do not commit adultery, and do not beat the child."
"2477","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \"Do not desire to fight the enemy, but pray to Allah for peace and prosperity, and when the enemy is confronted, then be steadfast and remember Allah often, and when they shout and call, be silent.\""
"2478","It was narrated from Sayyidna Sahib Rumi, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray during the campaign of Hunain: “Allahumma bik ahawil . . . ."
"2479","Sulaiman bin Burida narrated from his father, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, appointed someone as the leader of a platoon, he used to command him: \"When you meet a polytheist enemy, invite them to one of three things, accept whichever of these three qualities they accept and do not fight with them. do not waste), then ask them to move from their country to the country of the emigrants and tell them that if they do so, what (the right to benefit) is for the emigrants will also be given to them, and the punishments (for wrongdoings) given to the emigrants will also be given to them, and if they refuse to migrate, their order will be like that of the Muslim villagers, and the order of Allah that is issued to the Muslims will be issued to them and to them. There will be no share in booty or wealth acquired without war except in the condition that they fight against the Muslims, and if they refuse to convert to Islam, ask them to pay the jizya, if they agree to pay the jizya, then accept it and refrain from them (from killing them or their property, because they have become dhimmi and their lives and property are protected), and if they refuse to pay the jizya, then fight them with help from Allah, and if you Besiege the fort and the people of the fort ask you for the responsibility of Allah and His Messenger (i.e. ask for peace), then do not give the responsibility to Allah and His Messenger, but give the responsibility to yourself, your father and your companions, because if you break your responsibility or the responsibility of your forefathers, it is easier than if you break the responsibility of Allah and His Messenger, and if you besiege a fort and then the people of the castle want them to come out of the fort at the command of Allah, then this condition But do not drive them out, but ask them to go out only on your command, because you do not know whether you will be able to follow the command of Allah or not, then decide on them as you wish.\""
"2480","Al-Qamah said: I narrated this hadith to Muqatil bin Hayyan, so he said: This same hadith was narrated to me by Muslim bin Haysam from Sayyidna Numan bin Muqrin, may Allah be pleased with him, and he narrated the same from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"2481","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) did not fight any nation before inviting it (to Islam). \n Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Sufyan did not hear this hadith from Ibn Abi Najih. (That is, this tradition is disconnected)."
"2482","It was narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to attack (the enemy) at the time of the Fajr prayer and try to listen."
"2483","Sayyiduna Aws bin Abi Aws Thaqfi (RA) said: I attended the service of the Messenger of Allah (SAW) with a delegation of Banu Thaqif and I was in a corner of the dome in which there was no one except the Messenger of Allah (SAW). He was sleeping. Suddenly a companion came to him and whispered. He (peace be upon him) said: \"Go and kill him.\" He said: Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \"Does he not bear witness that there is no god but Allah?\" Shuba said: I doubt whether he said about the martyrdom of Muhammad. He said: Yes (he bears witness to this), he said: \"I have been ordered to fight against the people until they say La ilaha illa Allah, and when they say this, then their blood and their wealth are forbidden to me except for the right of Islam (i.e. limit or retribution), and their account is entrusted to Allah.\" The narrator said: This man killed Abu Mas'ud and death did not come to him until the best people of Taif died."
"2484","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"The blood of a Muslim who believes in the word la ilaha illa Allah (Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah) is not halal, but the blood of three people is halal: one who takes life for life, one who commits adultery after being married, and one who leaves Islam (apostate) and leaves the congregation.\""
"2485","Khalid bin Samir said: Abdullah bin Rabah Ansari came to us. The Ansar knew them as jurisprudents, they said: Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us a hadith that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an army of nobles, they marched and stayed as long as Allah willed, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit and gave the order, so it was announced: “Al-Salaat-e-Jami’ah” means the prayer is ready."
"2486","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"He who is consulted must be trustworthy.\""
"2487","Sayyidna Ka'b bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to fight somewhere, he used to do Turia (hiding it from others)."
"2488","Sayyidna Salama bin Aku'a said: I fought a man and killed him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me his property and on that day our code word with Sayyidna Khalid bin Al-Waleed was \"Ummat\" which means kill (kill)."
"2489","Sayyidina Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Fahri (RA) said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) in the Battle of Hunain on a hot day and we camped under the shade of trees. After that he narrated the whole story and told me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) filled his fist with clay and the person who was very close to him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me that he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw this clay at the enemies and said: \"Woe to their faces\", then Allah defeated the polytheists. \n Ya'ali said: Their sons narrated to me that their fathers said that there should not be one of us left at that time whose eyes and mouth are not filled with mud."
"2490","Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) said: We were in a meeting with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and he (PBUH) said to us: \"Pledge allegiance to me that you will not associate anyone with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery, nor kill your children, nor will you deliberately slander anyone, so whoever of you fulfills (this pledge), his reward is due to Allah, and If someone gets involved in one of these things (i.e. commits adultery, theft, etc.) and Allah hides his (sin), then his matter is in the hands of Allah. If He wills, He can punish him and if He wills, He can forgive him. So we pledged allegiance to you on these things."
"2491","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (may God be pleased with him) said: We were one thousand four hundred men on the occasion of Hudaybiyyah. We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and Sayyiduna Umar was holding his hand under the (shade) of a tree, it was a Samra (a wild tree that grows in the desert and is probably called the Kikar tree)."
"2492","Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) says: On the day of the Ahzab (trench) battle, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wash the mud with us, and because of the mud, the whiteness of his armpits was hidden, and he, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to hum these verses: \n (That is, \"O Allah! If it were not for Your guidance, we would never have found the straight path, we would not have been able to give charity, and we would not have prayed. Now, O Allah, give peace to our hearts, and keep us steadfast when we are surrounded by enemies.\" \n The enemies have abused us, whenever they want to make us fitna, we refuse“, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was reciting these verses aloud."
"2493","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah in the year of the conquest of Makkah, he placed himself on the blessed head of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Is this Ibn Khatl hanging from the curtains of the Kaaba? The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Kill him.\""
"2494","It was narrated on the authority of Anas that the handle of the Prophet's sword was made of silver. \n Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Hisham al-Dastawi opposed it, he narrated it from Qatadah on the authority of Saeed bin Abi al-Hasan and he narrated it on the authority of the Prophet, peace be upon him, and the people understood that this is safe."
"2495","Sayyidina Abu Talha (RA) narrated that when the Prophet (PBUH) conquered a people, he liked to stay in their land for three days."
"2496","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) burned the gardens of Banunazir."
"2497","Sayyidina Abu Huraira al-Dawsi (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) sent us on a campaign and said: \"If you succeed in capturing so-and-so, then burn them both in the fire.\" When it was the second day, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a messenger to us saying, \"I ordered you to burn these two men, but I think that it is not appropriate for anyone but Allah to make (someone) suffer the punishment of fire. If you catch them, kill them.\""
"2498","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: In some of the battles of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, a woman was found who had been killed, so seeing this, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade the killing of women and children."
"2499","Sayyidna Aswad bin Saari, may Allah be pleased with him, said: We went on a campaign with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and succeeded in arresting the idolaters. The people were quick to kill them and even started killing their children. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard about this, he said: \"What is the matter, some people have taken the killing and looting to such an extent that they start killing children too? Be careful not to kill children.\" He repeated this command three times. In some hadiths, there is the word \"La taqtulun\" which means \"never kill children.\""
"2500","Atiya al-Qurazi said: (On the day when the people of Bani Qurayza were killed) we were brought before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and the one whose hair had grown was killed and the one whose hair had not grown was left, and I was among those whose hair had not grown."
"2501","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \"Free the prisoner, feed the hungry.\""
"2502","It was narrated from Sayyidina Imran bin Hussain (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) released one man in exchange for two men (i.e. released one unbeliever in exchange for two Muslim prisoners)."
"2503",""
"2504","Sayyiduna Abu Wail (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided the booty of Hunain into Jaarana. Imam al-Darmi (may God have mercy on him) said: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may God be pleased with him) is among his isnaads."
"2505","Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layli narrated from his father, he said: I was present with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the time of the conquest of Khaybar. The polytheists were defeated. When we occupied their places of residence, the people rushed to the camels they found and immediately started boiling them in the pots, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered and all the pots were overturned. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided (the meat) between us and gave one goat to every ten people. Abu Laila said: There were only nine Banufals and I was alone. There was a goat for us too. \n Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: I have heard that Zayd bin Abi Anisa narrated this hadith from Qais bin Muslim, his purpose was that Zayd did not remember (this tradition is from the order) (but this is surprising on the part of Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, because Zayd may have heard it from the order and also from Qays bin Muslim)."
"2506","Zayd bin Abi Anisa on the authority of Qays bin Muslim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layli, on the authority of his father, and said: I turned to them (i.e. 9 persons). \n Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: The chain of transmission of Zakaria bin Adi is correct in my opinion."
"2507","Yazid bin Hurmuz said: Najda bin Amir wrote to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) and inquired about some things, so Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (RA) wrote in reply, \"Have you inquired about the share of relatives that Allah has mentioned (in the Qur'an)?\" We believed that the relatives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are the same relatives (i.e. we people), but our people denied it."
"2508","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave three shares (of booty) to the horseman and one share to the footmen on the day of Khaibar."
"2509","In this manner, the above-mentioned hadith is narrated. The translation is above."
"2510","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I was present with the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) at the time of the distribution of booty, he (may God bless him and grant him peace) gave me a share except on the day of Khaibar, which was special only for the people of Hudaybiyah, and Sayyiduna Abu Musa and Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) came between Hudaybiyah and Khaybar."
"2511","The freed slave of Umayr Abul Laham said: I was a slave (of my master) when I came (to the battle) in Khyber, so the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave me a sword from among his personal possessions and said: \"Hang it up.\""
"2512","It was narrated from Sayyidina Abu Umamah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling the shares before dividing them."
"2513","Hanash al-Sanaani narrated: We waged Jihad in the West and our Commander-in-Chief was Sayyidna Ruifa bin Thabit Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him). We conquered a village which used to be called Jarba, then Sayyidna Ruifa bin Thabit Ansari stood among us as a speaker and said: I stood among you because I heard from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"2514","It was narrated from Sayyidna Abul Darda' (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) saw a pregnant woman lying at the door of the tent and said: \"Perhaps her owner has intercourse with her?\" The people said: Yes, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"I wanted to curse him in such a way that he would accompany him to the grave. Why should he make his son his heir when he is not lawful for him? And how can he take service from him and he is not lawful for him?\""
"2515","It was narrated from Abu Abd al-Rahman Habli that Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (RA) was in an army and children and their mothers were separated. When he saw the children, they were crying, so he returned each child to its mother and he used to say: Verily, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \"He who separates his mother from her children, Allah will separate him from his friends on the Day of Resurrection.\""
"2516","Sayyidna Sakhr bin Aila (and some called Ghaila) said: I arrested the maternal grandmother of Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba Radi Allahu Anhu and took her to the service of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. Sayyidna Mughira, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, for his maternal grandmother. Hand it over to Mughira.” \n And Bani Salim had a spring of water. When he accepted Islam, he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and demanded its return. He (peace be upon him) called me and said: \"O Rock! When people accept Islam, they save their wealth and blood, return this (glasses) to them\", so I returned it."
"2517","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) sent a group in which Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) himself was also present."
"2518","Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) said that when the Prophet (PBUH) attacked the enemy's land, he would give a reward of one-fourth of the booty, and when all the people returned (and there was a need for war again), he would give a reward of one-third of the booty."
"2519","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Habib bin Muslimah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave an additional reward of one-third after Khums."
"2520","On the authority of Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever kills an unbeliever, the property of that slain person will be given to the one who killed him.\" Sayyiduna Abu Talha (RA) killed twenty men (infidels) on that day (in the Battle of Hunain) and took their goods and means."
"2521","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I fought with a disbelieving man and killed him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me his property."
"2522","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked rewards and said: \"A strong (powerful) Muslim should give away the booty to a weak Muslim.\""
"2523","It was narrated from Sayyidna Ubadah that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Pay even the needle and the thread and avoid betrayal, which will be a shame for those who betray on the Day of Resurrection.\""
"2524","Hanash Sanani said: We fought in the west with Sayyidna Ruifa bin Thabit Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, and we conquered a village called Jarba. At that time, Sayyidna Ruifa bin Thabit Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, stood among us to give a sermon, and said: I have stood among you at this time because I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, when he stood among us after Khaybar, he said: \"Whoever worships Allah and the Day of Resurrection.\" If he believes in the Hereafter, then he should not ride on the booty of the Muslims, and when he becomes weak, he should return it.” \n Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: I have doubts about \"Ridaha\". \n Then he said: \"And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not wear any cloth from the booty of the Muslims, even when it becomes rotten and old, he should return it to the treasury.\""
"2525","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: Sayyidna Umar Ibn Al-Khattab (RA) narrated to me the hadith that how many companions were martyred on the day of Khaibar. People started saying: So-and-so is a martyr until they mentioned a man that he is a martyr. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Not at all, I saw him in Hell in a robe or cloak which he had stolen from the booty\"."
"2526","Salim bin Abdullah narrated it from his father, from his grandfather Sayyiduna Umar. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"When you find someone who has stolen from the booty, take him away and burn his belongings.\""
"2527","Kathir bin Abdullah bin Umar bin Awf Muzni narrated from his father, he narrated from his grandfather Sayyiduna Amr bin Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"No robbery is permissible, no treachery, and no theft is permissible, and whoever steals will bring what he stole with him on the Day of Resurrection.\" \n Imam Abu Muhammad Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Asalal means theft."
"2528","Junada bin Abi Umayyah said, \"If I had not listened to Sayyidna Basr bin Arta'ah, may Allah be pleased with him, I would have cut off my hands.\""
"2529","Sayyidna Abu Hameed Sa'idi (RA) reported that the Prophet (PBUH) entrusted a worker with the responsibility of receiving charity. It is for you (i.e. the money of Bait al-Mal) and it was gifted to me (is wealth). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Then why don't you stay in your father's and mother's house, then see if you receive a gift there too?\" Then in the evening, after the prayer, the Prophet (peace be upon him) stood on the pulpit and gave a sermon, praising Allah as much as he could. Then he comes to us and says that this is your tax and it has been given to me, then why does he not sit in his parents' house and then see if he is given a gift or not? So he will bring it in such a situation that the voice of a cow will be coming, if it is the betrayal of a goat, then he will come in the situation that the voice of a goat will be coming, that's all I have conveyed to you. \n Sayyidina Abu Hameed (RA) said: Then the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) raised his hands so high that we began to see the whiteness of his armpits. Sayyidna Abu Hameed (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Along with me, Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) also heard this hadith from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Ask him."
"2530","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik (RA) that the king of Dhi-Yazn sent a gift to the Prophet (PBUH) by buying one halah for 33 camels or 33 camels, which the Prophet (PBUH) accepted."
"2531","Sayyidina Abu Hameed Sa'idi (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The ruler of Elah sent a letter to the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) and sent a gift of a white mule."
"2532","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"We do not take help from polytheists.\""
"2533","From this chain of narrators, Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated it in the same context."
"2534","Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah (RA) said: The last thing that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said was: \"Eliminate the Jews from the Hijaz and the people of Najran from the Arabian Peninsula.\""
"2535","Sayyidna Abu Tha'laba Khoshni (RA) narrated: I came to the service of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and said: O Messenger of Allah! We live in the land of people of the book, so can we eat from their dishes? The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Even if you live in such a land as you have described, do not eat from their vessel, except that there is no other choice (i.e. if you are forced and no vessel is found). If there is no other choice, then wash this vessel and then eat in it.\""
"2536","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughfil (RA) said: On the day of Khyber, a cup of fat was thrown, I came and grabbed it, and I said: I will not give anything from it to anyone today. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: It is hoped that Hameed (bin Hilal) heard this from Sayyidna Abdullah bin Mughfil (may God be pleased with him)."
"2537","Bajla said: Sayyiduna Umar did not take jizya from the Magi until Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf testified that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, took jizya from the Magi of Hijr."
